# GET - Load a file into memory

```text
GET [hex-address] filename
```

## Load and inspect

```text
GET D0:TEST.COM
PEEK 100 11F
```

GET defaults to address 0100H and returns to the command prompt. The
optional hex address selects a different starting point.
[PEEK](PEEK.HLP) lets you inspect the bytes in place.

## Execute

Use [GO](GO.HLP) for a program loaded at 0100H. Launching another
transient can overwrite the image. Use [JUMP](JUMP.HLP) when you know
the intended entry address.
